{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">RETRY function</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/310523","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/RETRY-function.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/RETRY-function.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"RETRY-function\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">RETRY function</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Returns a TRUE value if the current block is\nbeing reprocessed after a previous UNDO, RETRY.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RETRY-function__syntax_GC1A15S2702648\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d475058e96\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"RETRY-function__idGDO2WE2676028\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>RETRY</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RETRY-function__example_GC1A15T2702652\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d475058e122\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">This\nprocedure bypasses the display of the Customer data when the REPEAT\nblock is retried (if user changes the Customer data and does not specify\na country). When you run this procedure, notice that even though\nthe procedure has undone any data that you entered (if you did not\nspecify a country), the data still appears in the window. The data\nis saved in the screen buffers, but it is not stored in the Customer\nrecord buffer. If you do not use the RETRY function, the AVM reprocesses\nthe DISPLAY statement and displays the previous values for the Customer\nfields, overwriting the data that was entered in error.</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-retry.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"RETRY-function__idGDO2WF2676032\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>REPEAT:\n  PROMPT-FOR Customer.CustNum.\n  FIND Customer USING Customer.CustNum.\n\n  IF NOT <strong class=\"ph b\">RETRY </strong>THEN \n    DISPLAY Customer.Name Customer.Address Customer.City Customer.State\n      Customer.Country.\n  ELSE \n    DISPLAY Customer.Country.\n    \n  SET Customer.Name Customer.Address Customer.City Customer.State\n    Customer.Country.\n  IF Customer.Country = &quot;&quot; THEN UNDO, RETRY.\nEND.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RETRY-function__notes_GC1A15U2702658\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d475058e160\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\">\n        <li class=\"li\">Using\nthe RETRY function in a block turns off the default error processing,\nwhich result in no infinite loop protection for the block.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">For more information on retry processing, see <cite class=\"cite\">OpenEdge Getting\nStarted: ABL Essentials</cite>.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RETRY-function__see-also_GC1A15V2702664\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d475058e178\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"UNDO-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/UNDO-statement.html\">UNDO statement</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"REPOSITION-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/REPOSITION-statement.html\">REPOSITION statement</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"RETURN-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/RETURN-statement.html\">RETURN statement</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/310523","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1470,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"RETRY function","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/RETRY-function.html","type":"Manual"}